.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH trace 1  "trace " 
.SH NAME
trace \- Trace an element to its semantic origin
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrace\fR [\fB\-\-paths\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-compact\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIELEMENT_ID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trace an element to its semantic origin
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH INSPECTION
.TP
\fB\-\-paths\fR
Display explicit exhaustive path list instead of collapsed tree hierarchy
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-depth\fR \fI<MAX_DEPTH>\fR
Limit traversal depth to N relationship hops
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\fR
Display compact arrow\-joined path rendering
.TP
<\fIELEMENT_ID\fR>
Target element ID (UUID or prefix) to trace
